art with substantial stock on hand: 2421022 units of EV_battery and 1327622 units of FPGA. EV_battery inventory carries a holding cost of $9.387 per unit, a shortage cost of $35.588 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day, while FPGA inventory costs $8.721 per unit to hold, has a shortage penalty of $37.192 per unit, and is also reviewed every 1 day. On the demand side, ABB Industrial buys EV_battery, with orders arriving anywhere from 8.0 days to 45.0 days apart and each order fixed at 1092271.0 units. Customer shipments take 3.0 days, the item sells at $3137.318 per unit, payment comes between 16.0 days and 61.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. NXP Semiconductors purchases FPGA on a regular 37.0-day cycle, with demand fixed at 3165671.0 units per order; delivery to the customer takes 10.0 days, the selling price is $1050.577 per unit, payment lands between 40.0 days and 55.0 days, and this business also follows a lost-sales policy.

