ys. GlassCore Ltd. supplies carbon_fiber with an average lead time of 17.0 days, a cost of $41.645 per unit, net 51.0 days, and a maximum order size of 822400 units. PolymerSource handles epoxy_compound, shipping in 17.0 to 19.0 days, charging $255.557 per unit, offering payment in 52.0 to 81.0 days, and limiting deliveries to 258289 units. SiliconWorks supplies memory_chip with an exponential lead time averaging 2.0 days, at $390.021 per unit, with payment due 86.0 days after delivery and a capacity of 719752 units per order. Manufacturing is split across 3 sites plus 1 warehouse. The Production Center manages GPU, epoxy_compound, carbon_fiber, motor_assembly, and plastic_pellet inventory, and runs a bonding step that turns carbon_fiber, plastic_pellet, motor_assembly, and epoxy_compound into GPU in a cycle ranging from 7.0 to 13.0 days. That step depends on the Packaging Machine, which has capacity for 4 units, a fixed service time of 2.53 days, batching turned on at 75 units, a maximum wait of 16.744 days, and an operating cost of $5.169 per day. The Processing Unit manages power_module, lens_assembly, and camera, and its coating step converts power_module and lens_assembly into camera in exactly 19.0 days. The Pilot Line manages tablet, memory_chip, plastic_pellet, and epoxy_compound, assembling tablets from epoxy_compound, memory_chip, and plastic_pellet in anywhere from 15.0 to 29.0 days. Finished output from the Production Center, Processing Unit, and Pilot Line is sent on to the Logistics Center for GPU, camera, and tablet distribution. Starting stock is quite large in several areas: 289468 units of power_module, 2977798 units of lens_assembly, 929488 units of motor_assembly, 4518392 units of GPU, 1703451 units of camera, and 299681 units of tablet. Lens_assembly carries a holding cost of $2.048 per unit, a shortage cost of $32.051 per unit, and daily review every 1 day. Motor_assembly has a holding cost of $2.485 per unit, a shortage penalty of $28.48 per unit, and is also checked every 1 day. GPU inventory costs $2.558 per unit to hold, has a shortage cost of $6.404 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. Camera starts with 1703451 units, has a shortage cost of $24.674 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. Tablet begins at 299681 units, with holding cost of $7.977 per unit, shortage cost of $22.143 per unit, and a 1-day review cadence. On the customer side, Apple Supply buys GPU, placing orders with exponentially distributed interarrival times averaging 33.0 days; demand is centered around 3281470.0 units with variability of about 192445.0 units, promised lead time runs between 6.0 and 24.0 days, unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $2230.763 per unit, and payment comes 84.0 days after delivery. Infineon Technologies purchases camera with order arrivals averaging 24.0 days, demand around 3927174.0 units with variation of 415526.0 units, customer lead time of 9.0 to 10.0 days, a backorder policy, a selling price of $1952.94 per unit, and 12.0-day payment terms. Siemens Digital takes tablet orders every 21.0 days flat, each order for 1672174.0 units, with delivery expected in 10.0 to 15.0 days; if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost, the tablet sells at $4230.941 per unit, and customer payment arrives between 34.0 and 58.0 days. Structurally, the network links 5 suppliers — MegaSupply, GlassCore Ltd., PolymerSource, SiliconWorks, and NanoMaterials Inc. — to 4 facilities: Production Center, Processing Unit, Pilot Line, and Logistics Center. The model runs in days over a 200-day horizon, with 10 replications.

