ate, solder_paste, display_panel, and aluminum_sheet into SoC units, which are then moved on to Fulfillment Hub. The business starts with 3317344 units of display_panel in stock, reviewed every 1 day, with holding cost at $0.537 per unit and shortage cost at $42.27 per unit. Finished SoC inventory begins at 2786452 units, is also reviewed every 1 day, and carries $5.101 per unit in holding cost plus $45.121 per unit in shortage cost. Demand comes from two customers. Schneider Electric places SoC orders every 41.0 days flat, with order sizes ranging from 2865388.0 units to 2912870.0 units, expects delivery in 17.0 days, and operates under a backorder policy, so customers wait until stock is available. These sales go out at $3411.541 per unit, and cash is collected between 27.0 days and 63.0 days later. Ross Associates orders with exponentially spaced arrivals averaging 54.0 days, requests exactly 1544421.0 units each time, and has a 5.0-day customer lead time. For this account, available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost, with a selling price of $2735.431 per unit and customer payment arriving between 28.0 days and 62.0 days. The model runs for a 500-day horizon with 10 replications.

