, carries a holding cost of $3.827 per unit, and faces a shortage penalty of $0.011 per unit. Medical_device begins with 1336705 units, is also reviewed every 1 day, and has a shortage cost of $26.308 per unit. On the demand side, Samsung Electronics buys GPU, placing orders every 15.0 days to 34.0 days, with demand roughly 520429.0 units and variability of 129775.0 units. Customer delivery for Samsung takes between 17.0 days and 22.0 days, the selling price is $3950.685 per unit, and payment arrives in 51.0 days to 72.0 days; if stock is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Siemens Digital purchases medical_device with arrivals averaging 46.0 days, a fixed demand of 1768576.0 units, a customer lead time of exactly 28.0 days, and a selling price of $2183.334 per unit. Siemens pays 31.0 days after delivery, and when supply is insufficient, available units ship immediately while the balance is backordered. The model runs over a 730-day horizon, with 1 replication, and results are collected after a 30-day warm-up period.

