0499 units; transfers to the Integration Center are immediate. For steel_rod, MetalFab Inc. works with an exponential lead time averaging 19.0 weeks, a low unit cost of $12.711, fixed payment due 62.0 days after receipt, and a capacity cap of 192923 units per order, with immediate transfer to the Integration Center. CarbonSupply Co. offers steel_rod in a consistent 17.0-week lead time at $350.527 per unit with payment terms between 35.0 days and 81.0 days, also transferred immediately. Inside the network, the Integration Center manages tablet, steel_rod, frame_structure, and copper_wire inventory and runs a cutting step that turns copper_wire, frame_structure, and steel_rod into tablet in 17.0 to 25.0 weeks per cycle, using the Injection Molder. The Assembly Hub manages frame_structure, steel_rod, heat_sink, router, and copper_wire, and its fabrication step converts steel_rod, heat_sink, frame_structure, and copper_wire into router in a 14.0 to 23.0 week cycle. The Injection Molder has capacity for 2 units at a time, works for between 5.516 weeks and 9.403 weeks per job, costs $12.739 per week to operate, and is subject to breakdowns after exactly 448.568 weeks of uptime followed by 36.932 weeks of downtime. The Quality Scanner also has capacity for 2 units, takes exactly 7.085 weeks per job, and runs at $8.297 per week. Starting stocks are substantial: 1289118 units of heat_sink, 4096039 units of frame_structure, 4673941 units of tablet, and 2761337 units of router. Heat_sink inventory is reviewed every 1 week and carries a shortage penalty of $34.862 per unit. Frame_structure is also reviewed every 1 week, with a holding cost of $6.275 per unit and a shortage cost of $7.076 per unit. Router stock is reviewed every 1 week and has a holding cost of $8.489 per unit. Customer demand comes from two large accounts. NXP Semiconductors buys tablet, placing orders somewhere between every 8.0 weeks and 35.0 weeks, with demand centered around 3543267.0 units and varying by a