ts of router in inventory. Router shortages are especially expensive at $38.437 per unit, and that item is reviewed every 1 hour. On the demand side, Ross Associates buys smartphone, placing orders every 35.0 to 58.0 hours, with demand centered around 1675639.0 units and varying by about 290544.0 units. Customers are promised shipment in 18.0 hours, the selling price is $717.349 per unit, payment comes in 24.0 to 59.0 days, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Samsung Electronics purchases router on a tighter rhythm, with arrivals every 24.0 to 46.0 hours and a fixed demand of 3503748.0 units. Router orders are delivered in 2.0 to 23.0 hours, sold at $2341.752 per unit, and paid 54.0 days later; any unmet quantity is backordered rather than lost.

